we build a dynamic array like ArrayList from scratch based on static array,
we can not build static array easily on java, because we can not manipulate memory
(in python we can, but in java JVM do this)

Arrays are O(1) for find based on index (because of order on memory)
Arrays are O(n) on insert (in bad scenario)
Arrays are O(n) on delete (we should rearrange all elements)
Arrays are O(n) for find based on value

----------------------------

we build a Linked-List from scratch based on nothing!
we just use some obj that have pointer to next obj
so they are distributed all over the RAM

Linked-List are O(1) on EDGE elements (inset/delete/find on
                                       first and last elements)
Linked-List are O(n) to find (value or index)
linked-list are O(n) to delete value

Note: delete last item on undirectional linked-list is O(n)
      because we need to find the item before the last item

